# Sort every cube on the table by colour into its own fixed drop-off position, in
# a single call (detect all -> for each: pick -> place -> park). PREFERRED
# whenever the user wants to CLASSIFY / SORT coloured cubes into per-colour spots.
# Request: optional gripper tightness. The per-colour destinations are fixed
#          (configured in the skill), so the caller supplies no positions.
# Response: whether every detected cube was sorted, plus a human-readable message
#           listing each cube's outcome (placed at / failure step).
string gripper      # how tightly to close on each cube, 0.0 (open) / 0.5 (standard) / 1.0 (tightest); pass "" for the standard grasp (the normal case — ALWAYS supply this field, use "" when in doubt)
---
bool ok             # true iff every detected sortable cube was grasped AND released at its colour's spot
string message      # human-readable status: per-cube outcomes, or which step failed
